:: D05_Phone_Nolan [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Nolan's text spiral" "float" "assets/ui/phone/nolan-text-spiral.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>Forty minutes after the call, the texts start.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "ok I can't sleep now" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "what the hell is going on with you" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "are you in witness protection" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "did you join a cult" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "is it a sex thing" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "whatever it is I've probably seen weirder" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "remember when Deshawn ate that entire ghost pepper on a dare and we had to take him to urgent care" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "whatever you're about to tell me can't be worse than that" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "right?" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "marcus?" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "ok going to sleep for real now" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "but I'm coming tomorrow at 6 and I'm bringing beer and you better explain everything" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "love you bro" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "no homo" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "ok maybe a little homo" "">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "goodnight" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>Sixteen texts in forty minutes. Classic Nolan. He processes anxiety through volume. The more worried he is, the more he talks, a reverse relationship between fear and silence that makes him the worst person to ever play poker and the best person to have in a crisis.</p>

<p>I read them all. I don't respond to any of them. Not because I don't want to. Because anything I type right now is either a lie or a truth he's not ready for, and he deserves better than both.</p>

<p>Tomorrow. Six o'clock. Beer and a revelation.</p>

<p>I turn the phone face-down. The screen glows faintly against the nightstand. Nolan's contact photo catches light. Freshman year. Orientation shirts. Both of us grinning.</p>

<p>Tomorrow that grin is going to fall off his face like a painting off a wall.</p>

<p>Or it won't. Maybe it won't. Maybe Nolan, who once drove forty minutes at 2 AM to bring me Gatorade when I had food poisoning, who threatened to fight my student loan company on the phone like a suburban attorney, who sends "love you bro no homo ok maybe a little homo" at midnight on a Tuesday, maybe that Nolan will look at Mia and see Marcus underneath and decide the outside is just packaging.</p>

<p>Maybe.</p>

<p>I turn off the light. The fist on the ceiling disappears into dark.</p>

</div>

<<if not $nolanTextsRead>>
